       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 4000 mg per dose, four times daily, which is 16,000 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** the usual limit for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision (800 mg four times daily). Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** this order is 5 times the maximum. It could cause serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg** by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain or inflammation.\n- **800 mg** by mouth three or four times daily (2,400\u20133,200 mg/day), the upper end of the range.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. Because you're a student, it's also worth having your supervising resident or attending verify the final order. If you want ibuprofen for a particular indication, such as pain, fever, or inflammatory arthritis, tell me and I can help match the dose to it."
